//  ECLIPSE
//
// eclipse doesn't have an actual "find next instance of last search", but rather [⌘]+G finds next instance of
// selected text. Its [⌘]+OPTION+G is "find all text in workspace". To emulate this as closely as possible, we would
// swap [⌘]+G and [⌘]+OPTION+G to be FIND-UNDER and FIND-NEXT; but we won't because Sublime's native behavior matches
//  Intellij.
//
// //  FIND UNDER: [⌘]+G
// //  - sublime default: find_next
// , {"keys":["super+g"], "command":"find_under"}

// //  FIND NEXT: [⌘]+[⌥]+G
// //  - sublime default: find_under
// , {"keys":["super+alt+g"], "command":"find_next"}
